###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# The paper reports no training-cost or inference-cost figures.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Table I gives energies in meV without saying per atom or per cell, and does not name the evaluation set; values are encoded with the unit meV as printed. Correlation orders are encoded as bodyOrder = order + 1 (MACE-MP 'small' order 3, from-scratch MACE order 2, ACE order 4).
# - The foundation model is named only as MACE-MP 'small' (no release), so no registry model is linked; the fine-tuning relation is a string-valued setting. The from-scratch ACE and MACE models come from the group's earlier work and their full settings are not restated.
# - Not encoded: freeze depths f0, f3, f5, f6 and the 'medium' and 'large' variants, learning curves (2% to 100% of the data), delta-learning models, sticking probabilities and minimum-energy paths, and the whole Ti-Al-V application (CASTEP, PBE, ultrasoft pseudopotentials, 800 eV; errors only as learning curves).
# - Read from the arXiv v3 preprint; arXiv id matched by title and author.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
